From 66477248c133e20710f27cf2be2e77aa999a2d0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Radiarch Project <radiarch@invalid>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 21:39:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] GPU transport prototype: beamlet (influence-matrix) mode

Run_simulation_beamlet hands over to gpu_Run_simulation_beamlet when MCSQUARE_GPU=1 (3D, sparse dose output only).
Spots are simulated in groups that fit a dose-memory budget (MCSQUARE_GPU_DOSE_BYTES, default 4 GB), each spot of a
group with its own dose grid on the device; MCsquare's Generate_PBS_particle samples each spot's Num_Primaries from
its single-spot plan, in parallel over spots. PostProcess_Scoring's scaling, the threshold and the compaction run
on the device (Thrust, entries ordered by spot and voxel); the host writes the blocks export_Sparse_image and
Merge_Sparse_Files would write, straight into the merged Outputs/Sparse_Dose files, without per-spot temporary
files. Dose-to-water post-processing or segmentation fall back to post-processing on the host.
